Version: [current]
Command: monochange check

Validate configuration, changesets, and run manifest lint rules

[1m[97mUsage:[0m [93mmonochange check[0m [95m[OPTIONS][0m

[1m[96mOptions:[0m
  [93m-f[0m, [93m--fix[0m
          Automatically fix lint issues where possible

  [93m-e[0m, [93m--ecosystem[0m[95m [0m[95m<ECOSYSTEMS>[0m
          Limit linting to specific lint suites

      [93m--only[0m[95m [0m[95m<RULES>[0m
          Run only the specified lint rule ids

      [93m--format[0m[95m [0m[95m<format>[0m
          Output format
          
          [default: markdown]
          [possible values: text, json, markdown, md]

  [93m-v[0m, [93m--verbose[0m
          Show extra lint diagnostic details

      [93m--sha[0m
          Output only the commit SHA of the discovered release record

  [93m-h[0m, [93m--help[0m
          Print help

[1m[96mGlobal Options:[0m
  [93m-q[0m, [93m--quiet[0m
          Suppress stdout/stderr output and run in dry-run mode when supported

      [93m--progress-format[0m[95m [0m[95m<FORMAT>[0m
          Control progress output on stderr
          
          [possible values: auto, unicode, ascii, json]

      [93m--jq[0m[95m [0m[95m<EXPRESSION>[0m
          Filter JSON output with a jq-style expression, such as `.assets[].name`

      [93m--snapshot[0m
          Print a normalized JSON snapshot for this command subtree

Examples:
  monochange check
  monochange check --fix
  monochange check --ecosystem cargo,npm
  monochange check --only cargo/sorted-dependencies

Lint rules are configured in the top-level [lints] section of monochange.toml:

[lints]
  use = ["cargo/recommended", "npm/recommended"]

[lints.rules]
  "cargo/internal-dependency-workspace" = "error"
